@startuml
!include style/ail.puml
allowmixing
hide circle
hide empty methods
top to bottom direction
title G9 · Locate declarations in packages, then slots in callables
folder "example::canvas\nversion 1" as canvas_pkg #E8F3EB {
  class "Canvas\nresource declaration" as canvas {
    Opaque handle; lifetime contracts omitted
  }
  class "position\nfunction declaration" as position {
    canvas : Canvas (parameter; named receiver)
    result : Geometry::Point (result slot)
  }
  class "Filter\ncallback declaration" as filter {
    point : Geometry::Point (parameter)
    result : bool (result slot)
  }
  position -up-> canvas : member(@Canvas, instance)
  position -[hidden]right-> filter
}
folder "example::geometry\nversion 1" as geometry_pkg #E8F3EB {
  class "Point\nrecord declaration" as point {
    x : i32 (field)
    y : i32 (field)
  }
}
canvas_pkg -down-> geometry_pkg : imports as Geometry
legend bottom
  Folder = named, versioned package; compartmented box = declaration.
  A declaration belongs to its enclosing package; entries belong to their box.
  position and Canvas are package-level siblings; the labelled arrow associates them.
  Geometry::Point resolves through the import to Point in example::geometry.
  Read each callable's parameter and result within that callable's box.
  Filter is introduced in the next fragment. Contracts and other package items are omitted.
  Non-normative model: L2, L4–L5, C1. The example import digest is a placeholder.
endlegend
@enduml
